From: OE-Alliance contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Add one-switch STB verbose diagnostics to System logging

Expose player diagnostics at Basic settings level without an OSD overlay.
Preserve existing debug preferences and include bounded hardware clock/status
snapshots, decoder lifecycle and video plane placement in the normal Kodi log.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STB-specific player integration]

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index 63dc055..b594df2 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -26147,3 +26147,14 @@ msgstr ""
 msgctxt "#54216"
 msgid "This receiver uses one mode for Dolby Digital and DTS. Downmix decodes DTS to stereo PCM; passthrough sends DTS to a compatible receiver."
 msgstr ""
+
+#. STB player diagnostics, available at the Basic settings level
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#54300"
+msgid "Enable STB verbose debug logging"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#54301"
+msgid "Logs audio, video, FFmpeg, A/V timing, PVR, add-ons and hardware player status without a screen overlay. Enable before reproducing the problem. For startup problems, restart Kodi once. Save /media/hdd/.kodi/temp/kodi.log before restarting again; the previous log is kodi.old.log. Logs can contain private paths and stream URLs. Disable after testing: verbose logs grow quickly. Existing debug settings are preserved."
+msgstr ""
